## Summary

I injected `data-semtag-*` hints across every screen of this heritage-culture SPA (`WebTestBench_0063`, in `web_applications_hinted/`), following the spec in `hint-design.md`.

**Screens covered:**
- **Home (`/`, hero view)** — `Header.tsx`, `HeroSection.tsx`
- **Home (`/`, panorama view, `?view=panorama`)** — `Header.tsx`, `PanoramaViewer.tsx` (+ `HeritageOverlay.tsx` when a hotspot is clicked)
- **Heritage listing** (rendered on both home views) — `HeritageListing.tsx`, `HeritageCard.tsx`
- **Heritage detail (`/heritage/:id`)** — `HeritageDetail.tsx` (including its "item not found" branch)
- **404 page** — `NotFound.tsx`
- `Footer.tsx` and the unused `NavLink.tsx` were deliberately left unhinted (see below).

**Id namespaces introduced:** `header.*`, `hero.*`, `listing.*` (with `listing.grid` as the folded collection), `overlay.*`, `panorama.*` (with `panorama.hotspots` as the folded collection), `detail.*`, `notfound.*`.

**Collections folded properly (container + `.item.<slug>` keys):**
- `listing.grid` → `listing.grid.item.<heritage-id>` (title link, title observable, category observable) in `HeritageCard.tsx`
- `panorama.hotspots` → `panorama.hotspots.item.<heritage-id>` (hotspot buttons) in `PanoramaViewer.tsx`

**Collection I could not fold, and why:** the detail-page image thumbnails (`item.images.map`) have no stable domain key — images are a plain string array with no slug/id, only position. Per §7 rule 2, folding requires a stable key, never an array index, so I gave each thumbnail its own non-collection id (`detail.gallery.thumbnail.0/1/2`, `role="action"`, `controls="detail.gallery.image"`) instead of forcing a `.item.<index>` pattern that the linter (correctly) would flag.

**Deliberately left unhinted:** `Footer.tsx` — its links duplicate the already-hinted "categories" navigation and are decorative per the coverage rule; and marketing stat numbers in `HeroSection.tsx` (constant, non-interactive figures).

**Validation:**
- `validate-semtags.mjs src` → 44 hinted elements, **0 errors, 0 warnings**.
- Manually confirmed both collection containers are true DOM ancestors of their items, and that all template-literal ids (`item.id`, thumbnail `index`) stay unique at runtime and page-wide.
- `tsc --noEmit`, `npm run build` → clean/succeed.
- `npm run lint` → 4 errors / 7 warnings, but I verified by diffing against the un-hinted original (`web_applications/WebTestBench_0063`) that every one of these pre-exists in the source and is unrelated to my changes (an `as any` cast, two empty-interface shadcn components, and several fast-refresh warnings in shared UI primitives).

No behavior, styling, copy, or business logic was changed — only `data-semtag-*` attributes were added, all on native elements or shadcn components that already spread `...props` to their DOM root, so no component prop-widening was needed.

